===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰebʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|yifte}}, {{m|enm|ȝift}}, partly from {{inh|en|ang|ġift}}, {{m|ang|ġyft|t=giving, consideration, dowry, wedding}} and {{der|en|non|gipt|t=gift, present, wedding}}; both from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*giftiz|t=gift}}. Equivalent to {{affix|en|give|-t|id2=th}} (etymologically {{affix|en|yive|-t|id2=th}}).
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|fy|jefte|t=gift}}, {{cog|nl|gift|t=gift}} and its doublet {{m|nl|gif|t=poison}}, {{cog|de|Gift|t=poison}}, {{cog|lb|Gëft|t=poison}}, {{cog|wym|gejft}}, {{m|wym|gyjft|t=poison}}, {{cog|yi|גיפֿט|t=poison}}, {{cog|da,nb,nn,sv|gift|t=poison}}, {{cog|is|gift|t=gift}}. {{doublet|en|yift}}. Distantly related to {{cog|en|habit}}, from {{cog|la|habitus}}.
{{col-bottom}}

