===Noun===
{{wp|[[+|+ (present)]]}}
{{en-noun}}

# Something [[give]]n to another [[voluntarily]], without [[charge]].
#: {{ux|en| She gave him a cell phone as a birthday '''gift'''.}}
#* {{RQ:F. Herbert Dune|page=40|text=“I thank you for the '''gift''', Dr. Yueh,” Paul said, speaking formally. “It will be our secret. If there is a '''gift''' or favor you wish from me, please do not hesitate to ask.”<br>"I . . . need for nothing," Yueh said.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1974|lyricist=w:Jean-Loup Dabadie|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oyqXeegqIK0|artist=w:Jean Gabin|title=But Now I Know|passage=But now I know, but now I really know / Of only one thing I am truly very sure / Love is a '''gift''', love is a '''gift'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|title=Stop & Examine|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=71|text=She bought the model as a surprise '''gift''' for a friend who is a lifelong [[HST]] fan and railwayman, and who will soon be celebrating a milestone birthday.}}
# A [[talent]] or [[natural]] [[ability]].
#: {{ux|en|She had a '''gift''' for playing the flute.}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=“{{...}} it is not fair of you to bring against mankind double weapons! Dangerous enough you are as woman alone, without bringing to your aid those '''gifts''' of mind suited to problems which men have been accustomed to arrogate to themselves.”}}
# Something [[gain]]ed [[incidentally]], without [[effort]].
# The act, right, or power of giving or bestowing.
#: {{ux|en|The office is in the '''gift''' of the President.}}
# {{lb|en|Australia}} A [[footrace]], often a short one with a prize, sometimes with a handicap system whereby runners start from different positions based on their past performance.
